menu "Firmgen Telemetry"

    choice FG_TELEMETRY_PROFILE
        prompt "Telemetry profile"
        default FG_TELEMETRY_PROFILE_DEBUG
        help
            Telemetry is a development aid, so it is compiled in for debug
            builds and compiled out completely for production builds. This is
            a hard on/off, not a reduced rate: a shipping device must not put
            diagnostic traffic on its serial line at all. Switching this
            choice is all it takes to go from a dev board to a shipping
            build — no source changes.

        config FG_TELEMETRY_PROFILE_DEBUG
            bool "Debug (telemetry ON - 500 ms interval, full detail)"
            help
                Streams a JSON line every 500 ms: CPU, task count, heap,
                stack, uptime, plus PSRAM/temperature where available, and a
                one-time boot/reset-reason event at startup. Includes the
                top-tasks breakdown (per-task CPU% and stack high-water-mark)
                when CONFIG_FREERTOS_GENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS is enabled.

        config FG_TELEMETRY_PROFILE_PRODUCTION
            bool "Production (telemetry OFF - emits nothing)"
            help
                Emits NOTHING. The sampling task, the JSON emitters and the
                boot/reset event are all compiled out, so there is no serial
                traffic, no extra task or stack, and no sampling cost.

                This also overrides FG_PROTO_MONITOR below, which writes
                protocol events to the same serial stream.

                The Live Intelligence RTOS and Protocol panels cannot
                populate in this profile - that is expected, not a fault.
                Switch back to Debug and reflash to stream again.
    endchoice

    config FG_TELEMETRY_LOG_LEVEL
        int "Runtime log verbosity (esp_log_level_set, 0-5)"
        range 0 5
        default 3
        help
            Applied once at firmgen_telemetry_start() via
            esp_log_level_set("*", ...) — lets debug and production builds
            ship with different log verbosity from the same Kconfig switch
            that picks the telemetry profile above, without touching
            CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL (which requires a full rebuild of every
            translation unit). 0=None 1=Error 2=Warn 3=Info 4=Debug 5=Verbose.

    config FG_TELEMETRY_TEMP_SENSOR
        bool "Sample on-chip temperature sensor"
        default n
        depends on SOC_TEMP_SENSOR_SUPPORTED
        help
            Reads the internal temperature sensor each interval and includes
            a "health":{"temp_c":...} field in the JSON output (shown as
            "CPU Temp" in the RTOS panel).

            OFF by default: enabling it makes the component require the
            esp_driver_tsens driver, which would otherwise be pulled into
            projects that don't use it. Turn this on only when you want the
            CPU temperature reading. Also disable it if your application
            already installs the temperature sensor driver — ESP-IDF allows
            only one owner of that driver at a time.

    config FG_PROTO_MONITOR
        bool "Enable protocol bus monitor"
        default y
        help
            Ignored when the Production telemetry profile is selected above:
            production emits nothing, and this monitor writes to the same
            serial stream.

            Enables the firmgen_proto_monitor component. Call
            firmgen_proto_monitor_start() from app_main and use
            fg_proto_i2c() / fg_proto_spi() / fg_proto_uart() /
            fg_proto_wifi_rssi() / fg_proto_mqtt_pub() from your driver
            callbacks to log protocol activity to the Live Intelligence Panel.

endmenu
